{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And a man who touches.</b> At the time of contact he defiles garments — this means he does not defile garments." "<b>In his lying-place.</b> Rashi explained: this teaches about the lying-place that it is severe, etc. That is, the lying-place of a zav, even if the zav never touched it, is as severe as the zav himself; and contact that is not a lying-place is only offspring of impurity, as it is written: ״והנוגע בבשר הזב יכבס בגדיו״ etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:24.823411150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}